    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274-a1">

                <pb facs="0478" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg444"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Gaceta de
                            <placeName>Guatemala</placeName> of <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1870-02-26">February 26, 1870</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">ministry of foreign relations.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center">[Editorial.]</p>
                <p>As there has been circulating in public different versions of what occurred
                    between this government and the British legation, provoked by the conduct of
                    that legation in granting asylum to Don Miguel Garcia Granados, the President
                    has ordered the publication of that correspondence. We also publish the
                    communication of the British chargé d’affaires, in which he informs ns he has
                    obtained permission from his government to return to England, and with it the
                    reply of our minister of foreign relations.</p>
            </div>
